---
import Tunnel from '../../../layouts/Tunnel.astro';
import Choice from '../../../components/Choice.astro';
---
<Tunnel title="Step 3 - Format the USB | Save My Gig!" status="Critical · Recovery" red>
  <div class="step-label">Step 3 of 5</div>
  <h2 style="margin-bottom:1rem">USB format</h2>

  <!-- This is the screen that actually erases the drive, so the warning lives
       HERE, not only on /erase one screen back. Every tunnel screen is a real
       URL with a back button; arriving here cold is normal. Also the one
       honest exception to the never-format rule the run list drilled in, and
       saying so out loud is what keeps that rule trustworthy. -->
  <div class="alert-card" style="margin-bottom:1.25rem">
    <div style="font-size:20px" aria-hidden="true">⚠️</div>
    <div>
      <strong>This erases the drive completely.</strong> It is the one exception
      to the never-format rule, and it is safe only because tonight's tracks are
      now on the computer. Confirm the disk name and size before you touch
      anything, formatting the wrong disk is unrecoverable.
    </div>
  </div>

    <ul class="checklist">
    <li>Right-click the USB drive → <strong>Format</strong> (or Disk Utility on Mac).</li>
    <li>Windows only offers FAT32 up to 32GB in that dialog. Bigger stick: use the free <strong>guiformat</strong> tool, two minutes.</li>
    <li>Format: <span class="mono">FAT32</span>, not exFAT, not NTFS. Older CDJs refuse exFAT.</li>
    <li>Name: <span class="mono">SAVEMYGIG</span> (or anything you like)</li>
    <li>Quick format: OK</li>
    <li>Scheme: <span class="mono">Master Boot Record (MBR)</span></li>
  </ul>

  <div class="alert-card" style="margin-bottom:1.5rem">
    <div style="font-size:20px">⚠️</div>
    <div><strong>Do not remove the USB during formatting.</strong></div>
  </div>

  <p class="question">Has the USB been successfully formatted?</p>

  <Choice step="format"
    a={{ href: '/protocol/critical/copy-back', label: 'YES - USB IS FORMATTED' }}
    b={{ href: '/protocol/critical/no-erase', label: 'NO - THE FORMAT FAILS', desc: 'The drive is done, and it no longer matters: your set is on the computer. Any other stick finishes the job.' }}
  />
</Tunnel>
